"""
## Purpose and audience
Behavioural spec of the V4 agent attach EFFECTS and the release port arms that a real capacity owner can drive
(milestone_0023 part B, items d and g): the read-only helper admission check the service runs before the attach
archive, the step-driver port's first effect sub-step (helper prepare on a real signed helper request and a real
capacity journal), the rule that a forced release never prepares or begins, the RP expire arm on the monotonic
clock, and the port-call flags the step machine passes. Written for owners of the Linux Host service agent.
## Operator workflow
Run this one file with the self-hosted runner and read `SPEC FILE VERDICT`.
Status: AUTHORED, NOT_RUN (no runnable binary when written, 2026-11-17).
## Compatibility and limitations
CANNOT be built here, so NOT covered behaviourally (they stay structural in the release spec): the second effect
sub-step past its input check (helper begin + open core + adoption needs a SimpleContainerOwnerV2 with a live
provider), the S arms (cleanup, settle, session return), the geometry drain and the pane io Read/Write/Resize arms
(all need a ContainerPrimaryAttachSessionV1, whose transfer is a native owner no fixture can construct), and the
U' cancel itself past R (needs the helper row executing under a real begin). milestone_0031 drives, on a real helper
store of the fixture journal: the entry guard in admit, the U classification and U' recording a missing R.
## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A case that reports a helper lease or `begin_attempted` after a forced release means the release port started an
effect. A changed error string is a contract change.
"""
